# Keeps the Docker build context small and, more importantly, keeps a stale or host-specific
# local install out of the image - both Dockerfile and Dockerfile.worker rely on their own `pnpm
# install` inside the build (see their `deps` stage), not on whatever happens to exist on the
# machine running `docker build`. Without this, `COPY . .` in the builder stage would copy the
# host's local node_modules (a different platform/arch than the image's node:22-slim, absent
# entirely on a fresh checkout, or just stale) over the freshly-installed one, silently reverting
# exactly the fix Dockerfile's runner stage relies on.
node_modules
protocol/**/node_modules

.next
.git
.gitignore

test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
coverage

*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
